2. aruco2 (third_party/aruco2)
------------------------------
Licence:   Apache License, Version 2.0.
Text:      third_party/aruco2/LICENSE, which is byte-identical to this
           repository's LICENSE. It dates from upstream's initial commit.
Upstream:  https://github.com/rmsalinas/aruco2 -- the aruco2 library, in the
           repository of R. Muñoz-Salinas (GitHub: rmsalinas).
Submodule: https://github.com/ColDSnit/aruco2 -- a fork of upstream, pinned
           at commit 1091fb9. Its four commits on top of upstream commit
           8755035 add the Python wrapper (python/, a root pyproject.toml, and
           changes to CMakeLists.txt, README.md and .gitignore), add input
           checks to src/aruco2.cpp and src/aruco2_fractal.cpp, fix an
           image-edge bounds check in the latter, and restore the README's
           credit to ArUco Nano as upstream words it.


3. OpenCV runtime in a Windows build of aruco2
----------------------------------------------
Licence:   Apache License, Version 2.0.
Project:   OpenCV, maintained by the OpenCV team.
Text:      third_party/aruco2/python/OPENCV_LICENSE.txt, which states that its
           licence text is copied from the OpenCV 4.11.0 distribution used to
           build the aruco2 package.
Note:      The submodule's source contains no OpenCV binaries. When the wrapper
           is built on Windows, third_party/aruco2/CMakeLists.txt copies the
           release opencv_world*.dll files it finds through OpenCV_DIR into the
           built aruco2 package; OPENCV_LICENSE.txt is installed into the
           package on every platform. This is separate from the opencv-python
           package pyCamSet itself depends on (pyproject.toml, [project]
           dependencies).


